    "notes": "Inspected all9 portable views. The present-day Roman Forum ruin has three tall fluted columns, the northeastern low stump, curved broken entablature, a shorter marble cella sector, exposed-brick circular podium and three specifically mapped low masonry fragments. Initial picture interpretation was corrected: the stump moved to the northeastern mapped end, and the cella wall now stops inside the western bay so the western tall column stands open. The roofless centre and missing remainder of the historic colonnade remain absent. Bases, flutes, coarse Corinthian leaf/volute masses and sparse dentils are selected medium-fi geometry. Exact damage and carved ornament are approximate."
