    "notes": "Reviewed approximate full-site fit on the unchanged161-square/6m standard DEM. Eight mapped components retain raw east/south coordinates; three tall columns and the northeastern stump identify the signed northwest surviving sector. The cella wall ends inside the western open bay, while the broken entablature spans the tall columns. The circular occupied base is seated above original terrain, with retaining faces reaching below the lowest perimeter sample. Across2826 mesh-height/boundary probes, the top foundation clears native terrain by at least0.1476m, so no ground or water opening is needed. Full-site loading replaces all8 authored records and preserves2080 independent tile buildings exactly. All2702 independent records in the local extract were checked outside the replacement envelope;409 nearby records remain in source for inspection. Nine native water features retain127659.45095056188 square metres. Failure preserves all2088 native tile buildings and terrain; eviction frees geometry. Synthetic10m partial residency deliberately clips the circular podium and outer entablature, but preserves original ground under and outside the clipped model with no terrain opening. Partial architectural completeness is not claimed. The surrounding unmodeled Forum ruins use the existing generic procedural renderer and are not historical reconstructions. Heights, thresholds, damaged profiles and coarse DEM grade remain approximate."
  },
  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "notes": "Accepted for the specific medium-fi present-day Temple of Vesta ruin in the Roman Forum and approximate standard-map/DEM placement. Eight raw map component footprints and57 vertices remain intact; mapped column centres are preserved. Ordinary northwest and reverse photos determine which three columns retain full height, the northeastern stump and open western bay. These survival heights are not supplied by PMTiles. The occupied foundation is14.9m across; the ordinary article describes an approximately15m historic podium and20 original columns, which are context rather than a full reconstruction. Podium2.05m,10.35m entablature top above the occupied floor, curved profiles, surviving wall ends, low fragments and carving are picture-guided visualization estimates. All2826 original triangle-height/boundary probes leave at least0.1476m clearance beneath the opaque base; retaining faces join below the terrain. No terrain/water cutout is needed, including under partial residency. Synthetic10m loading intentionally clips the podium and entablature; complete architecture requires surrounding tiles, while the native ground stays intact. Independent Forum ruins retain the existing generic procedural appearance and are not historical reconstructions. Exact damage patterns, navigable interiors, buried chambers, the missing roof and the remainder of the former colonnade are outside scope. No bespoke survey or archival research was used."
  },
